			"Message": "style(Sky): Normalize em-dashes and consolidate Workbench table in README\n\nReplace em-dashes (`—`) with hyphens (`-`) throughout README.md for consistency with standard markdown conventions. Restructure the Key Features section to inline the Workbench Variants overview as a table, removing the duplicate standalone section. Simplify all markdown table header separators to use bare `---` without colons, matching minimal table syntax.\n\nNo functional impact — documentation formatting only.",
			"SHA": "ecf0b039ec0dd8ec3ae5db0fbfb8d1da4bb0c4bc"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T20:04:07Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⡏⠀⠀⠀",
				154,
				49
			],
			"Message": "style(Sky): Remove redundant blank lines after opening braces\n\nStrip the blank line that immediately follows opening `{`, `[`, and `(`\nthroughout the SkyBridge installers, workbench entry points, smoke-test\ndiagnostics, Astro config, Polyfills, OTELBridge, PostHog bridge,\nTraceparent bridge, env declarations, and both README/Doc files. The\nblank line served no structural purpose — it was left after the closing\n`}` blank line convention was enforced in the previous formatting pass\nbut the matching opening-brace rule was missed.\n\nAffects ~50 TypeScript source files plus DeepDive.md and README.md\n(the latter two get pure line-wrap rewrapping). The three dynamic\nimport expressions in Bootstrap.ts that were broken across two lines\nin commit 97432a68 revert to a single line because the surrounding\nindentation collapse no longer pushes them past the max-width limit.\n\nThe Extension Change Subscriber in Electron/Extension/Change/\nSubscriber.ts and the Bundled Electron entry see minor type-annotation\nreformatting driven by the same brace-byte-offset change.\n\nNo functional impact — whitespace only.",
			"SHA": "3d78380f701c301a658d9eb4072dd5d78edb6f3a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T19:12:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⡇⠀⠀⠀",
				154,
				47
			],
			"Message": "style(Sky): Enforce consistent blank lines across Bridge/workbench\n\nAdd a blank line before every interface property block, function/export body,\nif/try/catch block, and import group across ~40 Source files — the Bridge\nmodule installers, workbench entry points, smoke-test diagnostics, Astro\nconfig, and env type declarations. This enforces a consistent formatting\nconvention that visually separates logical code sections.\n\nThe one substantive change is the Extension Change Subscriber\n(`Source/Workbench/Electron/Extension/Change/Subscriber.ts`), which abandons\nthe Effect-TS stream pipeline (`Effect`, `EffectStream`, `runForEach`) in\nfavour of the simpler callback-based `WatchExtensionChanges` API now exposed\nby Wind's `Effect/Extensions/ChangeStream.ts`. The new approach stores a\ndisposable subscription handle and tears down any prior subscription before\nre-registering, preventing duplicate listeners on re-invocation.\n\nNo functional impact on runtime behaviour; the formatting changes are purely\ncosmetic and the subscriber refactor preserves the same external contract.",
			"SHA": "baf19de0ad189540a19390db1c2604879f9eca57"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:48:13Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				154,
				1
			],
			"Message": "style(Sky): Break long dynamic import lines in Electron Bootstrap\n\nThe dynamic `import()` call expressions in Bootstrap.ts exceeded the project's maximum line length. Wrap each long import argument — `runBootstrap` from Wind's Effect Bootstrap, the Extension Change Subscriber, and `InitializeWebSocket` from TauriMainProcessService — across two lines to match the project's formatting conventions.\n\nNo functional changes; code logic and execution order are preserved.",
			"SHA": "97432a6833c9caad70131df5d02a00ef35c5aa88"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:24:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				154,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Sky): Drop redundant Effect.runPromise wrapper from Wind bootstrap\n\nThe `runBootstrap` export from `@codeeditorland/wind/Target/Effect/Bootstrap` already returns a Promise, making the `Effect.runPromise()` wrapper and the corresponding `Effect` import a redundant indirection layer.\n\nRemove the unused `Effect` import from both `Electron/Bootstrap.ts` and `Mountain.astro`, and replace the `Effect.runPromise(runBootstrap(...))` call in Mountain.astro with a plain `await runBootstrap(...)`. Also add an inline comment in `InstallProgressTerminalWorkspace.ts` documenting how cancellable progress routes through `IProgressService.withProgress` on the workbench side.\n\nThe bootstrap path is now one async indirection leaner with one fewer runtime dependency import.",
			"SHA": "4a3290c96ab9823bbbff63d3051d4e62c5f6b0b7"
		}
	],
